course: dictionary
lesson: 5122
title: Invaders and context
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An invader is someone or something that goes into a place to take it over or cause harm. Look at the words around the word to check its meaning. Invaders often come with armies and by force.
explain: The same word is used in science. A cane toad or grey squirrel that spreads into a place where it does not belong is called an invader. The clue is the word science, plus the words animal or plant near it.
explain: «The immune system fights off invaders such as germs.» Germs are not soldiers, so invaders here means anything that enters the body and causes harm. Try your meaning in the sentence: does «fights off anything that enters the body and causes harm» still make sense? Yes, so you have it right.
fact: An invader is a person, army or country that enters another place by force to take it over.
fact: In science, an invader is a plant, animal or germ that spreads where it does not belong and causes harm.
fact: Britain had many invaders in history: Romans, Anglo-Saxons, Vikings and Normans.
fact: «An old idea that invaders destroyed the Indus cities suddenly is now not believed; the decline was slow.» This shows that people in the past did not always know the full story, so check what a word means in its sentence.
fact: Useful phrases are «Viking invaders» and «fight off the invaders», which means to push them back.
exercise: «Viking invaders sailed across the sea to raid the coast.» What is an invader? | *A person or army that enters a place by force to take it over | A friendly visitor who brings a gift | A kind of sailing boat | A type of fish
exercise: In science, what is an invader? | *A plant, animal or germ that spreads where it does not belong and causes harm | An animal that lives only in the sea | A plant that grows in a pot on a windowsill | A scientist who studies the stars
exercise: «The immune system fights off invaders such as germs.» What are the invaders in this sentence? | Off | The immune system | Fights | *Germs
test: In the game Space Invaders, the aliens attack. What does invaders mean in this game? | Spaceships that are parked | Players who lose the game | *Aliens that attack | Friendly helpers who play with you
test: What does «fight off» mean in «fight off the invaders»? | *Push back, so they have to leave | Join them in a game | Invite them in for tea | Hide from them forever
exam: Which best describes an invader? | A house with a red door | A kind of cheese | A song sung at school | *Someone who comes into a place where they are not wanted
